  "result": "`click.KeyValue` is implemented, and the full test suite passes (1916 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed). I haven't committed anything.\n\n- **Behavior:** `click.KeyValue()` splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")` and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`. Input with no `=` or with an empty key fails with `'ab' is not a valid key=value pair.` A tuple that is already converted passes through unchanged.\n- **Code:** the class is in `src/click/types.py` and exported from `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs:** it is added to `docs/api.md` and `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **Changelog:** 8.5.0 was already released on 2026-08-24, so I added a new \"Version 8.6.0 / Unreleased\" section to `CHANGES.md` with the entry. The class docstring says `versionadded:: 8.6` to match.\n- **Tests:** unit tests for good and bad input and a CliRunner test with `multiple=True` are in `tests/test_types.py`. There is also an entry in `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n- **Lint:** `ruff` auto-fixed one annotation in `types.py`, changing `t.Tuple` to `tuple`. I didn't run `mypy` because it isn't installed here.",
